    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d554-a13">

                <pb facs="0509" n="435" xml:id="pg435"/>

                <opener>[Enclosure L]</opener>
                <head>J Mr. Burling ame to Mr. McCartee</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-02-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 20, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your despatch of December 31, 1864, has
                    been received. It informs me of the successful settlement of one of the most
                    difficult cases ever presented for diplomatic action. Your conduct throughout
                    the negotiations is deserving of special commendation. The department will
                    learn, as I do, of your resignation with regret, and will appreciate your
                    patriotic efforts in the past, as well as your proffer of similar services in
                    the future.</p>
                <p>I shall have the honor to suggest your name to the government in connexion with a
                    place better suited than the one which you have had for the exercise of your
                    rare qualities as a Christian, patriot, and scholar.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ANSON BUKLINGAME.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>D. B. <hi rendition="#small-caps">McCartee,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chifu,</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
